Configure and run the debugger: Debugging support is provided by the Python Debugger extension, which is automatically installed with the Python extension. To ensure it has been installed correctly, open the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X) and search for @installed python debugger. You should see the Python Debugger extension listed in the results. Next, set a breakpoint on line 2 of hello.py by placing the cursor on the print call and pressing F9.


Install and use packages: In Python, packages are how you obtain any number of useful code libraries, typically from PyPI, that provide additional functionality to your program. For this example, you use the numpy package to generate a rando
